faqs:
  - q: "Which calendars does it sync with?"
    a: "GullStack booking syncs with Google Calendar, Microsoft Outlook, Apple Calendar (iCal), and any CalDAV-compatible calendar. Sync is real-time and bidirectional — when you block time on your personal calendar, those slots automatically become unavailable for booking. When a customer books, it instantly appears on your calendar."
  - q: "Can I send automatic reminders to reduce no-shows?"
    a: "Yes. You can configure email and SMS reminders at any interval — 24 hours before, 2 hours before, or whatever works for your business. Clients also receive an immediate confirmation when they book and a follow-up after their appointment. Businesses using our reminder system report a 30-40% reduction in no-shows."
  - q: "Can I require a deposit or full payment at booking?"
    a: "Absolutely. You can require a deposit, full payment, or no payment at booking — it is fully configurable by service type. Payment is processed at our 1% rate, and if a client no-shows, you already have their deposit. This is especially popular with salons, consultants, and therapists who lose revenue from cancellations."
  - q: "Does it support group bookings or classes?"
    a: "Yes. You can set up group sessions, classes, or workshops with a maximum capacity. Customers book individual spots, and the session automatically closes when it fills up. This works great for yoga studios, group therapy sessions, workshops, and fitness classes."
  - q: "Can multiple staff members have their own calendars?"
    a: "Yes. Each team member gets their own availability settings and booking page. Customers can book with a specific staff member or choose the first available person. This is ideal for salons, medical practices, and any business with multiple service providers."
